# Canonical author identities.
#
# Seventy commits accumulated six identities for two actual authors — a bare
# GitHub noreply address that does not link to the profile, a placeholder
# `mailt@example.com` from a misconfigured git user, a personal address, and
# two name variants. This file canonicalises them for `git log`, `git blame`,
# `git shortlog -sne`, and anything else that reads mailmap.
#
# Deliberately NOT a history rewrite: this repo is cloned onto every machine by
# the Claude Code plugin system, so a force-push would leave every marketplace
# clone diverged and needing manual repair, and would dangle every commit SHA
# recorded in memory/decisions/ and past PR bodies.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> <address-seen-in-history>
# A bare `Name <email>` line canonicalises the NAME for every commit already
# using that email.

Saptami K <79509062+ramsaptami@users.noreply.github.com>
Saptami K <79509062+ramsaptami@users.noreply.github.com> <ramsaptami@users.noreply.github.com>
Saptami K <79509062+ramsaptami@users.noreply.github.com> <ramsaptami@gmail.com>
Saptami K <79509062+ramsaptami@users.noreply.github.com> <mailt@example.com>

